.TH BYTE_HASH 3
.SH NAME
byte_hash \- compute a DJB2 hash of a byte array
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <byte.h>
.PP
.BI "uint32 byte_hash(const void* " x ", size_t " len ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B byte_hash
computes a 32-bit hash value for the byte array pointed to by
.I x
with length
.IR len .
.PP
The implementation uses the DJB2 algorithm, a widely known hash function designed by Dan Bernstein, which is efficient and produces good distribution for string and byte-array keys.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the computed 32-bit unsigned hash value.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR uint32 (3)